14. Lid self-adjointness: K(t,t') = A(t) conj(A(t'))
==================================================================
    max|K(t,t') - conj(K(t',t))| on [20,120]^2 grid:
      zeta     : 1.137e-13
      g (off)  : 1.972e-31
      h (line) : 0.000e+00

    NOTE: K = A(t)conj(A(t')) is a rank-1 Gram kernel --
    conj(K(t',t)) = conj(A(t')conj(A(t))) = A(t)conj(A(t'))
    identically for ANY f.  Hermiticity is automatic and
    carries no information about zero positions.
    verdict: TEST NOT SENSITIVE: rank-1 Gram kernel is identically Hermitian for all three functions

  14b. Reflection kernel K_R = A(t) - conj(A(-t'))
    function                         max|D|       max|S|
    zeta                         1.7919e+00   2.9496e+00
    xi (completed)               3.3138e-08   2.3452e-08
    g sym quartet                8.8818e-16   4.9878e-16
    g asym (0.6 pair only)       2.0000e+01   2.0000e+01
    h on-line                    2.2204e-16   1.1102e-16

    algebra: D(t,t') = S(t)-conj(S(t')), S=A(t)+A(-t);
    Schwarz gives S = 2 Re f'/f = 2 d(sigma) log|f| at 1/2.
    This vanishes iff f is symmetric under s->1-s on the
    line (exact FE) -- it is BLIND to FE-paired off-line
    zeros (their Re parts cancel) and nonzero for any
    f lacking exact line symmetry (zeta's chi factor).
    verdict: K_R detects FE-asymmetry, not off-line zeros: g_sym and xi read ~0, g_asym reads large, zeta reads nonzero via chi

